{
  "date": "2026-10-13",
  "id": "3727",
  "title": "Maximum Alternating Sum of Squares",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-alternating-sum-of-squares/",
  "topics": [
    "Array",
    "Greedy",
    "Sorting"
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "You are given an integer array nums. You may rearrange the elements in any order."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "The alternating score of an array arr is defined as:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• score = arr[0]^2 - arr[1]^2 + arr[2]^2 - arr[3]^2 + ..."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Return an integer denoting the maximum possible alternating score of nums after rearranging its elements."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Example 1:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Input: nums = [1,2,3]"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Output: 12"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "A possible rearrangement for nums is [2,1,3], which gives the maximum alternating score among all possible rearrangements."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "The alternating score is calculated as:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "score = 2^2 - 1^2 + 3^2 = 4 - 1 + 9 = 12"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Example 2:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Input: nums = [1,-1,2,-2,3,-3]"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Output: 16"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "A possible rearrangement for nums is [-3,-1,-2,1,3,2], which gives the maximum alternating score among all possible rearrangements."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "The alternating score is calculated as:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "score = (-3)^2 - (-1)^2 + (-2)^2 - (1)^2 + (3)^2 - (2)^2 = 9 - 1 + 4 - 1 + 9 - 4 = 16"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Constraints:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• 1 <= nums.length <= 10^5"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• -4 * 10^4 <= nums[i] <= 4 * 10^4"
    }
  ]
}
